      "sectionTitle": "Welcome to Dataiku GenAI Monitoring",
      "sectionText": "Several sections will help you configure the project and your data. You can check the requirements [here](article:15) and the [project setup tutorial](article:14)",
      "tiles": []
    },
    {
      "sectionTitle": "Configure your audit logs ingestion",
      "sectionText": "1. Select the logs origin.\n  - **To use log4j logs**, select *log4j logs* and select the connection on which you can access your logs. [More info about audit logs here.](https://doc.dataiku.com/dss/latest/operations/audit-trail/centralization-and-dispatch.html#log4j-target)\n  - **To use Event Server logs**, select *Event Server logs* and select the connection to the location of your [Event Server logs](https://doc.dataiku.com/dss/latest/operations/audit-trail/eventserver.html).\n  - **To use cloud instance logs**, select *Cloud logs* and select *dku-audit-log* connection as explained [here](https://doc.dataiku.com/dss/latest/operations/audit-trail/dataikucloud.html#access-instances-audit-logs).\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n2. **For production setup** requiring regular refresh, it is strongly recommended to configure the partitioning section. The smaller the partition period is, the faster and more responsive your monitoring experience will be.\n\u003cbr /\u003e\n3. Optionally, you can configure the engine used by visual recipes.\n3. Click on **RECONFIGURE** to apply your changes.",
